     "text": "{\"reachable\": false, \"rationale\": \"Blocking h1_2:escalate and h2_0:obtain cuts every path to the target. From the entry footholds, the attacker can still reach h1_0:access, h1_1:access and h2_2:traverse, but none of these lead further. h2_1:pivot has only one parent, h1_2:escalate, which is blocked. h3_0:escalate, h3_1:traverse and h3_2:access depend only on h1_2, h2_0 or h2_1, all of which are unreachable. With no h3 step reachable, h4_0, h4_1 and h4_2 cannot be reached. That leaves h5_0:reach and h5_1:pivot unreachable, so crown:obtain (OR of h5_0 and h5_1) is not reachable.\"}"
